<!--Post: 8401--><!--Time: 1109113283-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8401"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:hkenley@san.rr.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Chiefron<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Chiefron<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 22, 2005 - 3:01 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Rose Hill is about 5 miles east of Derby or about 10 miles south east of downtown Wichita. <BR> <BR>I do not know where you are going with that link though. All I see is a guy who served his country twice over, very honorably. I just don&#39;t see the connection. If we start looking for POI&#39;s based on posts on messages boards, whose source we cannot verify, we will have thousands of POI threads that boarder on being slander, especially in the case of an honorably retired Master Sgt. whose only similarity is tenuous at best. <BR> <BR>Ron<!--/Text--></td></tr>
