<!--Post: 8424--><!--Time: 1109122110-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8424"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:williammichael@direcway.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Oklahoma_mike<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Oklahoma_mike<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->11-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 22, 2005 - 5:28 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I&#39;m with Chiefron on this at least at the moment. I don&#39;t see anything linking this man to the crimes of btk.  In fact, I see the contrary. All the evidence about this USAF Sgt., retired, indicates he fit in well with whatever environment he operated.  Seems to have done way above average for a military man and as a civilian.  He also is a joiner, notice the several organizations he was a member of?  I do not think btk is this social of an animal, nor as confident in his career.  If he had done as well as this man, he would not want to kill. <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8424-->
<!--Post: 8449--><!--Time: 1109135148-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8449"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Pax56<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Pax56<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 22, 2005 - 9:05 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Also note that he&#39;s nuclear qualified.  People with even one of BTK&#39;s overt psychological traits don&#39;t get anywhere near nukes.  That does it for me - he&#39;s innocent.  Frankly, I&#39;d be proud if one of my kids grew up to be like this guy.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8449-->
<!--Post: 8476--><!--Time: 1109171702-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8476"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Ztargate<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ztargate<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 23, 2005 - 7:15 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Don&#39;t feel bad for posting the link. If we are going to stop posting possible POIs because someone thinks the person is all 100% honorable, then we might as well don&#39;t have a thread called POIs. <BR> <BR>Being a POI doesn&#39;t mean slander, because nobody is saying this is BTK. All they are saying is this is a &#34;Person Of Interest&#34;, let&#39;s look at him. <BR> <BR>That&#39;s what a discussion board is all about. <BR><IMG SRC="http://www.catchbtk.com/discus/clipart/happy.gif" ALT=":-&#41;" BORDER=0> <BR> <BR>p.s. <BR>I don&#39;t know how, I had come up with that link about three days ago... haha!<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8476-->
<!--Post: 8479--><!--Time: 1109173313-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8479"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Dpinva<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Dpinva<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 23, 2005 - 7:41 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->After this let&#39;s check out Jimmy Carter, Neil Diamond and the Pope. They are all in the age window and cannot be otherwise excluded. <BR> <BR>Leave this gentleman alone. He honorably served his nation, in two careers, and unless you have pictures of him leaving the Otero&#39;s house during a snowy day then I think you on the wrong track. <BR> <BR>I don&#39;t mean to sound a fecetious as I did in the start of this post, so I will ask. WHY, very specifically an explicitly, do you like this guy for BTK?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8479-->
<!--Post: 8499--><!--Time: 1109177702-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8499"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Cyndi<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Cyndi<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 23, 2005 - 8:55 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Dpinva, he didn&#39;t say he &#34;liked&#34; this POI.  He already stated his reasons for listing him in his above post.   Access to addresses, age range, etc. Just because someone has served their country honorably DOES NOT mean they are incapable of acting dishonorably.  I was the stepdaughter of a military person &#34;serving his country&#34; and trust me, he did some VERY dishonorable things while in service.   <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8499-->
<!--Post: 8500--><!--Time: 1109178228-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8500"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Ztargate<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ztargate<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 23, 2005 - 9:03 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->If we were not to discuss a person because we don&#39;t have pictures of them leaving the Otero house, then we might as well don&#39;t discuss anybody at all. Because not even the police has such pictures.  <BR> <BR>NOBODY is saying the guy is BTK. He meets some criteria and that&#39;s why he mentioned it.... to discuss it.......  <BR> <BR>Nothing else. <BR> <BR>Hello! <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8500-->
<!--Post: 8512--><!--Time: 1109180888-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8512"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:hkenley@san.rr.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Chiefron<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Chiefron<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 23, 2005 - 9:48 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Maybe you misunderstand me. Nutzger posted that one of his reasons for suspecting this POI was that:  <BR> <BR>&#34;he said something like smelling the flowers makes his day????? in one of his posts.&#34; <BR> <BR>Strike that one reason and you have a person who was a postal worker and in the right age group. Why strike that statement? Because there is no credible evidence that the person who posted that is BTK. So working from what is known and not from what is speculated, you have a guy who is in the range and who was a postal worker. <BR> <BR>I don&#39;t want you to not have him as a POI, but unless you have something more substantial, I would suggest sharing your ideas privately with people rather than plastering his name on internet web sites under suspect threads. <BR> <BR>I have researched dozens of POIs, a few of whom are still in my mind POI, yet I have not connected any of them enough with fact to warrant a post for general consumption.  <BR> <BR>You do realize that using your criteria for establishing someone as a POI, you might as well just ask WPD to go swab everyone who worked for USPS in Sedgewick county between 1973 and 2005?  <BR> <BR>Narrow it down, provide at least 1 compelling argument for, and then post.  <BR> <BR>Ron  <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8512-->
<!--Post: 8518--><!--Time: 1109182744-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8518"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Ztargate<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ztargate<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 23, 2005 - 10:19 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Okay, here it goes. This is what makes that Goetz guy a POI. <BR> <BR>1. James A. Goetz grew up in Indiana ..... close state. <BR> <BR>2. Joined the U.S. Air Force in 1952.... right age, military service. <BR> <BR>3. He received initial training on electronic fundamentals..... basic electronics, could fix copiers and small appliances. <BR> <BR>4. Upon graduation was selected for nuclear weapons electronics and mechanical training..... mechanical engineering book reference to one of his letters left in the library.  <BR> <BR>5. He came to Kansas as a member of the 36th Aviation Depot Squadron at Smoky Hill &#40;later renamed Schilling&#41; Air Force Base, Salina..... he lived in the area. <BR> <BR>6. He qualified in both nuclear and conventional weapons handling, including explosive ordnance disposal....... he knew how to use a gun. <BR> <BR>7. Goetz was discharged in 1957 and joined the Air Force Reserve while beginning what proved to be a 31-year career with the U.S. Postal Service........... there we go, some thought BTK once was somehow related to the post office. <BR> <BR>8. He came into the Kansas Air National Guard in 1965 with the 190th Tactical Reconnaissance Group in Hutchinson and blah blah blah........ he remained in the area for many years. <BR> <BR>9. While in the reserve, his other assignments included supervisor of vehicle maintenance and a second tour as NCOIC of disaster preparedness..... like teaching how to tie knots and secure stuff. <BR> <BR>10. Being from Indiana, he was still in Kansas in 1988, Goetz was promoted to chief master sergeant and was appointed senior enlisted advisor &#40;SEA&#41; for the Kansas Air National Guard, the top enlisted position in the state. <BR> <BR>&#40;should I mention there is a National Guard armory right across the street from where the Oteros used to live?&#41; <BR> <BR>11. He actively promoted resident school attendance of Professional Military Education &#40;PME&#41; courses such as Leadership School, NCO Academy, and the Senior NCO Academy......... this would match the &#34;leadership&#34; voice on the Nancy Fox call that many talk about. <BR> <BR>12. Goetz is now retired from both the Air Guard and the Postal Service, living in Rose Hill with his wife, Marilyn...... which would explain his amount of free time to do BTK hauntings stuff. <BR> <BR>I AM NOT SAYING THAT THIS MAN IS BTK.  <BR> <BR>I am merely telling you all who are telling others not to post links or talk about anyone who are not shown coming out of the Otero home, that this is a forum to discuss &#34;persons of interest&#34; and you should not be asking others not to post about a certain person because the person doesn&#39;t seem btkish to you. <BR> <BR>That said in the nicest way. <BR> <BR><IMG SRC="http://www.catchbtk.com/discus/clipart/happy.gif" ALT=":-&#41;" BORDER=0> <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
