<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8576"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:nugzter@yahoo.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Nugzter<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Nugzter<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 23, 2005 - 6:12 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->i think so too. but to pull it off in the same city is tough, he had to have had a &#34;normal&#34; side. he may have went to prostitues and played what ever roll he wanted. double life, tripple life, quadrupel life. it is for sure he is as evil as 4 people combined.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8576-->
<!--Post: 8591--><!--Time: 1109218034-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8591"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Ztargate<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ztargate<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 23, 2005 - 8:07 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Dpinva, nobody is saying &#34;This is BTK&#34;. His name was mentioned as a POSSIBLE POI, in order to discuss him in the thread.  <BR> <BR>Without a name or reference to a link which has his name, then we cannot discuss ANY POI. <BR> <BR>Many people here, not me, have mentioned BY NAME the chief of police, the different detectives, the anchors of the two main TV stations in the area, even some of the victims, as POIs. And, nobody cried &#34;slander&#34;. <BR> <BR>Besides, to prove slander one has to show maliciousness. And, clearly, there is no maliciousness in discussing him.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8591-->
<!--Post: 8593--><!--Time: 1109218647-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8593"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Ztargate<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ztargate<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 23, 2005 - 8:17 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Embersage, how can we discuss a POI without saying who it is? Isn&#39;t that what this forum is for? This is ridiculous. <BR> <BR>Why ask us to email the names of a POI in private?  <BR> <BR>Again, we are merely discussing a person... clearly not saying the person is BTK. <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8593-->
<!--Post: 8682--><!--Time: 1109282994-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8682"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Dpinva<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Dpinva<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 24, 2005 - 2:09 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text--><i>Many people here, not me, have mentioned BY NAME the chief of police, the different detectives, the anchors of the two main TV stations in the area, even some of the victims, as POIs. And, nobody cried &#34;slander&#34;. </i> <BR> <BR>All of these individuals are in the public domain and are, to one degree or another public figures. Public figures, both legally and ethically, have to meet a much higher threshold before they can claim slander. This gentleman is a private citizen with no public profile at all. To name him in this context is, if not slander, at least slanderous. If you really don&#39;t think it is a problem to mention people&#39;s names and discuss them, although the clearly are not BTK, then what is <i>your name</i>? I am sure you won&#39;t mind us posting it on the internet so we can &#34;discuss&#34; you as well, right? <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8682-->
<!--Post: 8702--><!--Time: 1109293372-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8702"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Ztargate<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ztargate<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 24, 2005 - 5:02 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I live hundreds of miles away from Wichita, never been to any state near Kansas, was a child when the crimes occurred, besides other more obvious things...  <BR> <BR>I guess it would serve no purpose to name me a POI, but if you want to discuss me as a POI, then you find my name first. <BR> <BR>As to the public figures having a higher threshold for slander, that is not so. We all have reputations and when someone makes false malicious statements about us, which ruin our good reputation, then that is slander... no matter if it&#39;s a public person or a private person.  <BR> <BR>But, if there were to be a difference, then it would make sense that a public figure may be more concerned about keeping a good reputation, than a private person. Specially when it affects the person&#39;s potential to earn a living. <BR> <BR>So, the way you put it, all the police officials, media persons, university employees, etc... whose names have been included in POIs discussions have no reason to cry slander and can be discussed... but then you cry slander when we talk about this guy? <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8702-->
<!--Post: 8713--><!--Time: 1109295288-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8713"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Freya<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Freya<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 24, 2005 - 5:34 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Ztargate, I believe Dpvina was actually referring to legal precedent that public officials have to prove actual malice when suing for slander&#40;spoken&#41; or libel &#40;written&#41; defamation. Private citizens may have a hard time proving damages to reputation, but generally they have an easier time suing for defamation than public officials. One premise for this is that public officials willingly put themselves in the spotlight, while private citizens go about their business privately and that privacy should be respected. <BR> <BR>I understand that it may seem harmless to discuss him on this board, and it may in fact be so. But ethically and legally, it&#39;s not a good idea to write someone else&#39;s name out on a board like this.  <BR> <BR>I honestly don&#39;t mean to berate you, I just don&#39;t want anyone to get in trouble on here for 1&#41; what he writes or 2&#41; what is written about him.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8713-->
<!--Post: 8720--><!--Time: 1109296541-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8720"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:embersageblue@aol.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Embersage<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Embersage<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 24, 2005 - 5:55 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I believe the question has been answered quite well by others. If you want to talk POI, protect the innocent.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8720-->
<!--Post: 8723--><!--Time: 1109298012-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8723"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Freya<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Freya<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 24, 2005 - 6:20 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->&#34;So, the way you put it, all the police officials, media persons, university employees, etc... whose names have been included in POIs discussions have no reason to cry slander and can be discussed... but then you cry slander when we talk about this guy?&#34; <BR> <BR>That question, as far as I could read, had not been answered in legal terms. Now it is.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8723-->
<!--Post: 8759--><!--Time: 1109309754-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8759"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Ztargate<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ztargate<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 24, 2005 - 9:35 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->AGAIN, I have seen people posting the REAL ACTUAL names of many police officers &#40;whether they were actually involved in the investigation or not&#41;, the names of university employees, and anchors of television stations, and the names of other businesses and citizens, on this board and being discussed. Yet, we cannot discuss this guy? <BR> <BR>Embersage says, &#34;If you want to talk POI, protect the innocent&#34;. <BR> <BR>Okay, so how do we know who is innocent? And how can we discuss a POI without using his name??????? LMAO! <BR> <BR>In order to discuss a POI, we have to have a name, because if we don&#39;t have a name, then the people reading won&#39;t have an idea of who the ell we are talking about. <BR> <BR>Anyway, I will leave it alone, since I&#39;m repeating myself. I guess others will continue to bring in POIs AND THEIR NAMES, and they will be discussed... just not this guy. <BR> <BR>Hmph! <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8759-->
<!--Post: 9051--><!--Time: 1109387136-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9051"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:hkenley@san.rr.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Chiefron<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Chiefron<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 25, 2005 - 7:05 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Guess you were wrong. Start apologizing. <BR> <BR>Ron<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9051-->
<!--Post: 9153--><!--Time: 1109403545-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9153"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Dpinva<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Dpinva<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 25, 2005 - 11:39 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Freya explained what I said very well. A person who benfits from a public profile legally &#40;and in my view morally and ethically&#41; has a much higher burden to claim defamation or slander, and a much lower expectation of privacy. <BR>This gentleman was minding his own business and was, as it turns out, incorrectly named by someone who had no reasonable reason to name him as a POI. And since Dennis Rader is now clearly BTK with 2 different DNA profile matches against him, this IS by definition slander <i>and </i>defamation of this individual&#39;s reputation and character, which was dragged through the mud here for reasons that I simply just don&#39;t get - you accomplished nothing in naming him except to begin a self agrandizing &#34;discussion&#34; in which you repeatedly tried to show us how much smarter you are than the rest of us. You failed in every apparent objective of naming this gentleman. <BR>I think you at the <u><i>absolute very least</i></u> owe him and the others you named &#40;if any&#41; an apology. And BTW, I never named ANYONE as a POI, so I am at a total loss about your assertion that I am naming police officers, etc. What <i>are </i>you refering to with that part?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9153-->
<!--Post: 9163--><!--Time: 1109405417-->
